      "slug": "top-down-crown-g230",
      "term": "Top-down crown",
      "definition": "Starting at the top of the hat with a magic ring and a small number of stitches, then increasing on every round until the hat is wide enough to sit on the head. The crown shaping is built in from the start."
    },
    {
      "slug": "dc2tog-g230",
      "term": "Dc2tog",
      "definition": "Double crochet two stitches together. Used in the top-down method to add only as many increases per round as are needed to keep the crown flat before the sides begin."
    }
  ],
